---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Faq from '../../components/Faq.astro';
import { pageByPath } from '../../lib/pages';
import { articleJsonLd, faqJsonLd } from '../../lib/jsonld';
import { PRIVACY_FAQS } from '../../lib/copy';

const page = pageByPath('/privacy/')!;

const faqs = PRIVACY_FAQS;
---
<Base title={page.title} description={page.description} path={page.path} jsonLd={[articleJsonLd(page), faqJsonLd(faqs)]}>
  <h1>Security and privacy</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    B4WeMeet is built so that we cannot see your job search — not "we choose not to look", but architecturally
    cannot. This page explains exactly how that works.
  </p>

  <h2>Your prep stays on your device</h2>
  <p>
    Everything you create in the Prep Pack builder — packs, stories, your pitch, research notes, debriefs — is
    stored in your browser's local storage (IndexedDB) on the device you are using. There is no B4WeMeet server
    database for user content, no account system, and no sync. Our servers deliver the pages and the tool; what
    you type into the tool never travels back.
  </p>
  <p>
    Two consequences worth understanding. First, your prep is tied to this browser: a different browser or
    device starts empty unless you import a backup. Second, clearing this site's browser data erases your prep
    — so export a backup from the tool's Backup &amp; storage tab and keep it somewhere private. The file
    contains your job search in plain text.
  </p>

  <h2>AI is bring-your-own</h2>
  <p>
    The mock-prep and polish features work by copying a pack to <em>your</em> clipboard and opening ChatGPT or
    Claude in a new tab with a short coaching prompt. You paste the pack yourself, into your own AI account.
    B4WeMeet holds no AI keys and sends nothing to any AI service.
  </p>

  <h2>Downloads are files, not links</h2>
  <p>
    Briefs, checklists, calendar files and backups are generated in your browser and downloaded as files. We
    never publish your content at a b4wemeet.app address, and there is no share link for your prep.
  </p>

  <h2>Site analytics</h2>
  <p>
    This site uses Dataflare, an analytics tool we self-host in our own Cloudflare account. It is cookieless —
    it sets no cookies and stores nothing on your device. It records pageviews, the referring site, and basic
    device and browser information so we can understand which content is useful. Analytics data is kept for 90
    days and is never sold or shared. It measures pages, not people, and it has no access to anything you
    prepare in the tool.
  </p>

  <h2>What changed in November 2026</h2>
  <p>
    Hosted intro pages were retired in November 2026 when B4WeMeet became a private, on-device tool. The
    previous version of B4WeMeet hosted public intro pages on our servers; that system — accounts-by-link,
    stored profiles, photos and all — has been shut down and its data deleted, because a tool people trust with
    something as sensitive as a job search should not be holding it on a server at all.
  </p>

  <Faq faqs={faqs} />
</Base>
